judgements.simplerVersion:
Two lines instead of four, and delete the duplicated path rather than adding it. Fail on ANY skipped, unconditionally:
  grep -qE '^ *Tests .*skipped' "$log" && { printf 'FAIL tests: N skipped -- a reference guard drifted or a test is parked. Not a pass.\n'; exit 1; }
No -d probe, so nothing to silently switch the guard off; and 'you may not COMMIT with a skipped test' stands on its own merits. The bare-clone case is unaffected because it never commits through this hook -- the session log shows the clean-clone check running npx vitest run directly.
